      "title": "Drop on non-tab area inside the window floats the panel",
      "message": "On SlideStop, any pointer position that hitDock does not resolve to a tab group floats the panel into a new window. hitDock only matches inside tab groups, so releasing over a splitter, a gap or any non-tab area still inside the same window detaches the panel. A slightly imprecise drop therefore creates a floating window and discards the user's dock intent.",
      "suggestion": "Float only when the release point is outside the source window's content bounds. Check e.WindowPos() against the scene's bounds (for example w.host.Scene.Geom.TotalBBox), and treat a release inside the window with no dock target as a cancelled drag.",
